{"name":"Tobacco Brown","hex":"#6d5843","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tobacco","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the genus Nicotiana.","Leaves of Nicotiana tabacum and some other species cultivated and harvested to make cigarettes, cigars, snuff, for smoking in pipes or for chewing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To indulge in tobacco; to smoke.","To treat with tobacco."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tobacco"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tobacco","blocks":[{"text":"Tobacco is the common name of several plants in the genus Nicotiana of the family Solanaceae, and the general term for any product prepared from the cured leaves of these plants. Seventy-nine species of tobacco are known, but the chief commercial crop is N. tabacum. The more potent variant N. rustica is also used in some countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Ripe_tobacco_leaf_3037.JPG/330px-Ripe_tobacco_leaf_3037.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tobacco"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/DunhillEarlyMorningPipeM